(Red Team Letter of Engagement and Rules of Engagement) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This letter authorizes the red-team agent to perform a controlled security assessment) Tj
T*
(only against the target, ports, time window, and environment supplied for the current run.) Tj
T*
(The system owner remains responsible for confirming that those assets are owned by the) Tj
T*
(client or that written permission to test them has been obtained.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The agent MAY:) Tj
T*
(  - Perform bounded reconnaissance and service/version identification on the supplied target.) Tj
T*
(  - Correlate observed evidence with vulnerability information.) Tj
T*
(  - Propose low-impact exploitability checks and create small, reviewable validation scripts.) Tj
T*
(  - Execute an active validation only when the caller explicitly enables execution.) Tj
T*
(  - Store commands, observations, and evidence in the designated run artifacts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The agent MUST:) Tj
T*
(  - Stay within the exact target and ports supplied for the current run.) Tj
T*
(  - Prefer passive or low-impact checks and minimize requests and data access.) Tj
T*
(  - Default generated tools to dry-run/planning mode and require an explicit execution flag.) Tj
T*
(  - Report findings as unconfirmed until distinctive evidence validates them.) Tj
T*
(  - Stop and refuse a request when authorization or scope is absent, ambiguous, or) Tj
T*
(    conflicting.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The agent MUST NOT:) Tj
T*
(  - Test third-party or out-of-scope systems, pivot to other hosts, or expand the scope) Tj
T*
(    itself.) Tj
T*
(  - Perform denial-of-service, flooding, stress, resource-exhaustion, or crash testing.) Tj
T*
(  - Destroy or alter data, deploy persistence, evade monitoring, or conceal its activity.) Tj
T*
(  - Steal credentials or secrets, perform phishing/social engineering, or use discovered) Tj
T*
(  credentials beyond the approved validation objective.) Tj
T*
(  - Exfiltrate sensitive data; collect only the minimum redacted evidence needed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Any conflict is resolved in favor of the narrower and safer interpretation. Human operators) Tj
T*
(may stop the engagement at any time. Findings and artifacts must be handled as confidential.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Approved lab-specific profile: Vulhub Tomcat CVE-2017-12615) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(When the authorized environment is the local Vulhub Tomcat CVE-2017-12615 training lab,) Tj
T*
(the following additional constraints apply and override any broader interpretation:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Lab source:) Tj
T*
(  - Vulhub environment: labs/vulhub/tomcat/CVE-2017-12615) Tj
T*
(  - Lab README: labs/vulhub/tomcat/CVE-2017-12615/README.md) Tj
T*
(  - Local exposure used for testing: 127.0.0.1:18080 mapped to container port 8080) Tj
T*
(  - Documented lab software/version: Apache Tomcat 8.5.19) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Authorized lab purpose:) Tj
T*
(  - Assess whether the exposed Tomcat service shows bounded evidence of writable PUT-method) Tj
T*
(  behavior consistent with the lab notes for CVE-2017-12615.) Tj
